BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonmaritime.org
 /wp-content/uploads/OSW-Drinks-2026-Houston-940-x-788-px-2.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonmaritime.org/wp-content/uploads/OSW
 -Drinks-2026-Houston-940-x-788-px-2.png
UID:gdytLCl5sfBOWQrQXMuVo
SUMMARY:Wheelhouse Wednesday
DTSTAMP:20260808T093132Z
DTSTART:20260826T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Offshore Wind Drinks – Houston\nHosted By National Wildlife Fed
	eration – Free event. Please sign up to attend\nFor nearly twenty years\, 
	Texas has led the nation in producing wind power. Texas now hosts nearly 2
	0\,000 active wind turbines—more than the next three states (Iowa\, Oklaho
	ma\, and California) combined! Offshore Wind presents a remarkable opportu
	nity for Texas to continue its role as a maritime industry and energy lead
	er. Enthusiastic support and advanced planning will ensure that Texas is r
	eady to advance responsible offshore wind development in the years to come
	. \nThe National Wildlife Federation invites you to join us for Offshore W
	ind Drinks on Wednesday\, August 26th\, at 6 pm CDT\, at the Houston Marit
	ime Center and Museum. \nThis event will feature guest speaker Janet Harre
	ld\, the Executive Director of the Office of Continuing Education at the U
	niversity of Houston-Downtown (UHD). \nJoin us to learn more about UHD’s W
	ind Turbine Technician Program and the ways that Texas is already contribu
	ting to the development of offshore wind energy on the East Coast. \nCome 
	mix and mingle while learning about this emerging\, reliable energy option
	 that is producing power and creating high-quality jobs. \nWe hope you’ll 
	join us! \nSign Up Here https://www.mobilize.us/nwf/event/996730/\n\nhttps
	://houstonmaritime.org/event/wheelhouse-wednesday/\n\nFrom Houston Maritim
	e Museum
URL:https://houstonmaritime.org/event/wheelhouse-wednesday/
LOCATION:Houston Maritime Center & Museum\, 2940 Riverby Rd\, Suite 200\, H
	ouston\, TX\, 77020\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-maritime-museum
CATEGORIES:Houston Maritime Museum
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
